","gene_symbol_current":"SERAC1","gene_id":"ENSG00000122335","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"higher in AD","nucleus_padj":0.528964,"nucleus_log2fc":0.0165175,"nucleus_score":0.888974,"pct_ad":0.150611,"pct_control":0.144115,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":0.0180722,"donor_lfcse":0.0853109,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":2.5896e-06,"degas_log2fc":-0.241034,"degas_padj":0.00142413},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"SERAC1","gene_symbol_current":"SERAC1","gene_id":"ENSG00000122335","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":1.24771e-05,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0849243,"nucleus_score":-4.52374,"pct_ad":0.204916,"pct_control":0.220046,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.965009,"donor_log2fc":-0.0326622,"donor_lfcse":0.0954135,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00352935,"degas_log2fc":-0.171712,"degas_padj":2.18087e-11}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000122335","module":"blue","kme":0.11929,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.137528,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000122335","entrez_id":["84947"],"uniprot":["Q96JX3"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is a phosphatidylglycerol remodeling protein found at the interface of mitochondria and endoplasmic reticula, where it mediates phospholipid exchange. The encoded protein plays a major role in mitochondrial function and intracellular cholesterol trafficking. Defects in this gene are a cause of 3-methylglutaconic aciduria with deafness, encephalopathy, and Leigh-like syndrome (MEGDEL). Two transcript variants, one protein-coding and the other non-protein coding, have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Aug 2012].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q96JX3","text":"Facilitates the transport of serine from the cytosol to the mitochondria by interacting with and stabilizing Sideroflexin-1 (SFXN1), a mitochondrial serine transporter, playing a fundamental role in the one-carbon cycle responsible for the synthesis of nucleotides needed for mitochondrial DNA replication (PubMed:35235340). Plays an important role in the phosphatidylglycerol (PG) remodeling that is essential for both mitochondrial function and intracellular cholesterol trafficking (PubMed:22683713). Specifically involved in the exchange of the sn-1 acyl chain from PG 16:0/18:1(9Z) (also known as 1-hexadecanoyl-2-(9Z-octadecenoyl)-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1'-sn-glycerol)) to PG 18:0/18:1(9Z) (also known as 1-octadecanoyl-2-(9Z-octadecenoyl)-sn-glycero-3-phospho-(1'-sn-glycerol)), a step needed in the bis(monoacylglycerol)phosphate biosynthetic pathway (PubMed:22683713). May have acyltransferase activity although the mechanism for PG remodeling has not been determined (PubMed:22683713)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}